# Copy to .env for local development.

# --- Server-side, and genuinely secret -------------------------------------
# These are read by the Netlify functions at request time. They have no VITE_
# prefix on purpose: Vite inlines any VITE_* variable into the browser bundle,
# which would publish them. `netlify dev` picks them up from this file; plain
# `vite dev` serves no /api/* routes at all, so use mock mode there instead.

# The fal.ai key this deployment generates with. Images, video and the
# "Improve with AI" buttons all run on it, and visitors supply no key of their
# own — which means every generation is billed to whoever sets this.
# FAL_KEY=

# REQUIRED for sign-in. Netlify Identity says who someone is; Supabase will not
# take its word for it, because row-level security only trusts tokens signed
# with the project's own key. `/api/session` signs one — see
# netlify/lib/supabaseToken.ts — and that same token is what the fal proxy
# verifies, so without this secret nobody can sign in and nobody can generate.
#
# Supabase → Project settings → API → JWT keys → the legacy JWT secret. It has
# no VITE_ fallback and must never gain one: inlining it into the bundle would
# let any visitor mint a session as anybody.
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=

# Which Supabase project this site belongs to. Falls back to VITE_SUPABASE_URL
# below — the same public string — so this is only worth setting to point the
# server at a different project.
# SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxx.supabase.co

# REQUIRED for Google Drive, which is the step straight after signing in. The
# consent screen returns a code that only these two can turn into a stored
# connection, so without them the editor cannot open.
#
# The client secret belongs to the same OAuth client as VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
# (Google console → Credentials → your Web application client). The service role
# key is under Supabase → Project settings → API; it bypasses row-level
# security, which is what lets the function read a table no browser can.
# Run supabase/migrations/0002_google_connections.sql first.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Only if a proxy rewrites the host in front of this site. The redirect URI is
# otherwise derived from the request, and must match the one registered in the
# Google console. NETLIFY_IDENTITY_URL is the same idea for the Identity
# endpoint, which is otherwise assumed to be on this site's own origin.
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://your-site.example/oauth/google
# NETLIFY_IDENTITY_URL=https://your-site.example/.netlify/identity

# Skips the session check on /api/fal/* entirely, for running `netlify dev`
# against a checkout with no Supabase project. Never set this on a deployed
# site: it leaves the endpoint open for anyone who finds the URL to generate
# video on your account.
# FAL_PROXY_ALLOW_ANONYMOUS=1

# --- Build-time, and not secret --------------------------------------------
# These ship in the bundle by design. All optional.

# Fakes every provider call locally, so no keys and no network are needed.
# VITE_MOCK_PROVIDERS=1

# Google OAuth client ID (type: Web application). This is Drive only now —
# signing in goes through Netlify Identity, which holds its own Google client in
# the Netlify dashboard. Leave unset to build without Drive. Not a secret — it
# ships in the bundle, and origin allowlisting is what protects it. See the
# README for the setup steps.
# VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxx.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Google API key and Cloud project number, for the Google Picker — which is how
# the user chooses their folder and imports existing media. Without the key
# there is no way to pick a folder, so the editor cannot open. Neither is a
# secret: restrict the key by HTTP referrer in the Cloud console. Enable the
# "Google Picker API" there alongside the Drive API.
# VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# VITE_GOOGLE_PROJECT_NUMBER=

# Supabase project, where timelines are saved. Set both to enable cloud
# projects; leave both unset to run purely against this browser's storage.
# The anon key is public by design — row-level security is what protects data.
# VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxx.supabase.co
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...

# Where Netlify Identity lives. Defaults to /.netlify/identity on whatever
# origin the app is served from, which is right for every deployed site and for
# `netlify dev`. Set it only for plain `npm run dev` on :5173, which has no
# Netlify behind it — point it at a deployed site to sign in locally.
# VITE_NETLIFY_IDENTITY_URL=https://your-site.netlify.app/.netlify/identity
